Requirement Analysis – StudentHub Portal

1. Project Overview

StudentHub Portal is a simple web-based application designed for students to manage their 
academic activities in one place. It provides a user-friendly interface where students can 
register, log in, and access important information such as attendance, assignments, timetable, results, and courses.

2. Project Objective

The main objective of the StudentHub Portal is to:

- Provide a central platform for students.
- Allow students to register and log in securely.
- Help students manage academic information easily.
- Reduce the time required to access different student services.

3. Functional Requirements

Home Page
- Display the portal title.
- Show a welcome message.
- Provide a brief description of the portal.
- Display links to the Login and Register pages.

Registration
- Allow new students to create an account.
- Collect the following information:
  - Full Name
  - Email Address
  - Username
  - Password
  - Confirm Password
- Validate user input before registration.

Login
- Allow registered students to log in using their username or email and password.
- Verify user credentials.
- Display an error message if the credentials are incorrect.

Student Dashboard (Future Enhancement)
After successful login, students should be able to:
- View attendance.
- View assignments.
- Check timetable.
- View examination results.
- Access course information.

Navigation
- Users should be able to navigate easily between the Home, Login, and Register pages.

4. Non-Functional Requirements

Usability
The website should have a clean and simple interface that is easy for students to use.

Performance
Pages should load quickly and respond smoothly.

Security
User passwords should be protected, and only authenticated users should be able to access student information.

Reliability
The application should function without unexpected errors.

Responsiveness
The website should work properly on desktops, tablets, and mobile devices.

### Maintainability
The project should be easy to update and maintain in the future.

5. User Requirements

The user should be able to:

- Open the StudentHub Portal.
- Read the portal information.
- Register as a new student.
- Log in using valid credentials.
- Access student-related information after login.

6. System Requirements

Hardware Requirements
- Computer or Laptop
- Keyboard and Mouse
- Internet Connection

Software Requirements
- HTML5
- CSS3
- JavaScript (optional)
- Visual Studio Code
- Modern Web Browser (Chrome, Firefox, Edge)

7. Input Requirements

The system accepts the following inputs:

- Full Name
- Email Address
- Username
- Password
- Confirm Password

8. Output Requirements

The system provides the following outputs:

- Welcome page
- Registration success message
- Login success or error message
- Student dashboard after successful login

9. Constraints

- Only registered users can log in.
- Username or email should be unique.
- Password and Confirm Password must match.
- All required fields must be completed before form submission.

10. Assumptions

- Every student has a valid email address.
- Users have access to the internet.
- The portal is intended only for students.

11. Future Scope

The following features can be added in future versions:

- Student profile management.
- Password recovery.
- Online assignment submission.
- Attendance analytics.
- Course registration.
- Notifications and announcements.
- Faculty and admin modules.
- Student feedback system.

12. Conclusion

StudentHub Portal is a basic student management web application that allows students to register, log in, and access academic information from a single platform. The system is designed to be simple, secure, responsive, and easy to use, making academic management more convenient for students.